// Using @where clause for constraints
// NOTE: This example is currently broken because #range generates string symbols
// and numeric comparisons like x > 2 don't work with strings.

#symbols(#range(1, 5))

// For all x where x > 2, P(x) holds
// BROKEN: x is a string like '1', '2', not an integer
// @forall x @where x > 2: P(x)

// There exists x where x != 1 and P(x)
@exists x @where x != 1: P(x)

// Complex where condition
// BROKEN: numeric comparison with string symbols
// @forall x @where x > 1 & x < 4: Q(x)
